v1.3.3 (2026-05-11)
-------------------
Completed end-to-end automated YubiKey registration flow:

Registration flow:
- register.html: certificate is now generated automatically on page load
  (no separate "Generate Certificate" button); user sees a single action:
  "Program my YubiKey"
- register.html: success panel now branches on ovpn_imported — if the helper
  auto-imported the .ovpn into OpenVPN Connect, shows "profile imported,
  open OpenVPN Connect and enter your PIN"; otherwise shows manual download
  button
- register.html: onHelperLaunch() polls every 2s for up to 30s after user
  clicks "Start VPN Helper" so the page reacts immediately when helper starts
- vpnweb-helper.py: after programming the YubiKey, downloads the .ovpn and
  opens it via os.startfile() (Windows file association → OpenVPN Connect);
  returns ovpn_imported: true/false in the /setup response

Installer:
- setup.nsi: pre-starts vpnweb-helper.py at end of install (via pythonw)
  so helper is already running when user clicks the registration link
- setup.nsi: updated finish message — "Insert your YubiKey, then open the
  registration link from your email"
- setup.nsi: fixed ${StrRep} → ${GetParent} (FileFunc.nsh); StrRep is not
  a built-in NSIS macro
- VPNSetup.exe: 174 KB compiled installer, served at /static/VPNSetup.exe

Email:
- Invite email redesigned: Step 1 = installer download link, Step 2 =
  registration link; clear instructions matching the automated flow
- HTML email: styled two-step layout with download button and registration
  link button

v1.3.2 (2026-05-11)
-------------------
Security hardening, bug fixes, YubiKey browser-based automated registration:

Security fixes:
- Fixed: XSS — hub names, usernames, group names and session names in the
  admin UI are now HTML-escaped before insertion into innerHTML
- Fixed: path traversal — hub/username values are validated against a safe
  name regex and path is resolve()-checked against CERTS_DIR
- Fixed: race condition — p12 download validates and marks token used
  atomically inside _tokens_lock
- Fixed: token reuse — issuing a new invite revokes all outstanding unused
  tokens for the same hub/user
- Fixed: cookie SameSite changed from "lax" to "strict"
- Fixed: sensitive JSON files written with 0o600 permissions
- Added: rclone remote path validated against allowlist regex before saving

YubiKey browser registration (backend):
- GET /api/register/{token}/p12-raw — raw p12 bytes, no used-marking
- GET /api/register/{token}/puk — system PUK, token-gated
- POST /api/register/{token}/complete — marks token used, records YubiKey in
  registry, sends PIN email
- GET/PUT /api/config/puk — admin can view/set the system PUK

YubiKey registry:
- yubikey_registry.json: each programmed YubiKey recorded with PUK, timestamp,
  username, hub; full history per serial kept on re-registration
- GET /api/config/yubikeys — per-serial PUK history for admin UI
- Settings UI: YubiKey Registry card with serial, last user, PUK (hidden by
  default), expandable history

Cloud backup (rclone):
- Replaced Google Drive API / service account with rclone (simpler auth,
  supports all cloud providers)
- GET/PUT /api/config/backup, POST /api/config/backup/run
- Auto-backup after each successful registration; manual "Backup Now" button
- rclone remote path validated before saving

Installer (setup.nsi / VPNSetup.exe):
- NSIS Windows installer: downloads and installs Python 3.12, Yubico PIV
  Tool, OpenVPN Connect if not present
- pip install flask yubikey-manager requests cryptography
- Copies libykcs11.dll to OpenVPN Connect pkcs11_modules/
- Registers vpnreg: URI scheme to launch helper from browser
- Creates Add/Remove Programs entry

